WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.500
InkBoard: a public board of poems, in Ghanaian
languages and English. Here's how it works.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.052
InkBoard is a public board
of poems, grouped by author.

3
00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:12.367
Drag to wander. Hold ⌘ or
Ctrl and scroll to zoom.

4
00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:16.556
Each section is one author.
Their poems sit inside as cards.

5
00:00:16.606 --> 00:00:19.642
Fit shows the whole board again;
the minimap shows where you are.

6
00:00:19.692 --> 00:00:22.242
Chapter 1: Reading. Wander the board, open a poem,
unlock a private one, search, browse by language.

7
00:00:22.346 --> 00:00:26.096
Click a poem to read
it right on the board.

8
00:00:26.146 --> 00:00:35.797
Poems can belong to a
collection: this is part 3 of 4.

9
00:00:35.847 --> 00:00:39.019
Step through the collection
without leaving the board.

10
00:00:39.069 --> 00:00:42.531
Every poem also has its own page and link.

11
00:00:42.581 --> 00:00:47.074
A collection has a page too,
with its poems in reading order.

12
00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:52.681
Private poems show only their
title. The text stays locked.

13
00:00:52.731 --> 00:00:55.903
Readers who have the
password can unlock it.

14
00:00:55.953 --> 00:00:59.859
Unlocked: the poem opens, and
stays open on this device.

15
00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:02.556
Search finds authors and poem titles.

16
00:01:02.606 --> 00:01:06.231
No special keyboard
needed: “agbo” finds Agbɔ.

17
00:01:06.281 --> 00:01:09.901
Pick a result and the
board takes you there.

18
00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:13.801
Browse by language: Akan (Twi,
Fante, Nzema), Ewe and Ga.

19
00:01:13.851 --> 00:01:18.472
Letters such as ɛ, ɔ, ɖ and ŋ
show properly, in every view.

20
00:01:18.522 --> 00:01:21.114
Akan covers Twi, Fante and Nzema.

21
00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:24.780
And Ga.

22
00:01:24.885 --> 00:01:28.056
Click an author's name to open their page.

23
00:01:28.106 --> 00:01:32.146
A tagline, a bio, links and
an avatar the author picks.

24
00:01:32.196 --> 00:01:36.316
Their pinned poem comes
first, then all their poems.

25
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.400
Chapter 2: Follow, share, install. Feeds, share
cards, the app on your phone, and reading offline.

26
00:01:39.506 --> 00:01:42.967
Subscribe to follow new
poems in any feed reader.

27
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:47.034
Each author has a feed of their own, too.

28
00:01:47.886 --> 00:01:56.019
Share a poem's link anywhere: it shows a card
with the title, the author and the opening lines.

29
00:01:56.129 --> 00:02:00.885
Coming back often? InkBoard
offers to go on your home screen.

30
00:02:00.935 --> 00:02:05.616
Confirm in your browser, and it
opens full screen, like an app.

31
00:02:05.722 --> 00:02:09.428
Every poem you open is
saved on your phone.

32
00:02:09.478 --> 00:02:17.410
No connection? The board and the
poems you've read still open.

33
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.500
Chapter 3: Writing. Sign in with a code, write
in Ewe, Akan, Ga or English, and publish.

34
00:02:20.655 --> 00:02:24.405
Writers sign in with their
email. No password to remember.

35
00:02:24.455 --> 00:02:28.787
A 6-digit code arrives by email.
Type it in, and you're in.

36
00:02:28.837 --> 00:02:32.588
The first time, choose the
pen name readers will see.

37
00:02:32.638 --> 00:02:35.386
That's it: this is your dashboard.

38
00:02:35.495 --> 00:02:38.377
Write a new poem from your dashboard.

39
00:02:38.427 --> 00:02:44.901
This one is in Ewe: “Ŋdi”, good morning.

40
00:02:44.951 --> 00:02:51.904
The special letters bar types Ewe,
Akan and Ga letters, and tone marks.

41
00:02:51.954 --> 00:02:54.547
Light formatting too:
*asterisks* make italics.

42
00:02:54.597 --> 00:02:59.221
Set its language, so readers can
find it when they browse by language.

43
00:02:59.271 --> 00:03:03.206
Save a draft: only you can see it.

44
00:03:03.256 --> 00:03:06.427
When it's ready, publish it to the board.

45
00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:10.019
Back on your list,
marked “Just published”.

46
00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:20.820
Any poem can be public, or
private behind a password.

47
00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:25.347
Readers see its title, and
need the password to read it.

48
00:03:25.397 --> 00:03:32.517
Or use one shared password for all
your private poems, in Settings.

49
00:03:32.628 --> 00:03:40.396
Edit a poem any time. Saving
updates it on the board right away.

50
00:03:40.446 --> 00:03:45.454
Every save keeps the version
before it, under History.

51
00:03:45.504 --> 00:03:48.385
Open one to see what changed since.

52
00:03:48.435 --> 00:03:53.219
Restore it, and it goes back
into the editor. Save to keep it.

53
00:03:53.329 --> 00:03:59.930
Collections group your poems
into an ordered sequence.

54
00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:06.058
Add poems to it…

55
00:04:06.108 --> 00:04:09.569
…and put them in the
order readers will follow.

56
00:04:09.619 --> 00:04:14.512
Readers then see each poem's
place in it: Part 1 of 3.

57
00:04:14.619 --> 00:04:24.981
Your profile is your author page: an
avatar, a tagline, a bio and links.

58
00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:28.856
Pin the poem you want
readers to see first.

59
00:04:28.906 --> 00:04:34.429
This is what readers see.

60
00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:37.533
Chapter 4: Signing in without email. Recovery
codes, passkeys, and computers that aren't yours.

61
00:04:37.661 --> 00:04:41.993
No email to hand? Make recovery
codes while you still have it.

62
00:04:42.043 --> 00:04:49.059
Ten codes, each good once. Keep them
in a password manager or your wallet.

63
00:04:49.109 --> 00:04:54.078
On another computer, sign in
with your email and one code.

64
00:04:54.128 --> 00:04:58.750
Then add a passkey: next time it's
just your fingerprint, face or PIN.

65
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:04.402
Signing in with a passkey:
no email, no code.

66
00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:09.395
On a shared or library computer,
tick “This isn't my device”.

67
00:05:09.445 --> 00:05:14.384
That sign-in ends when the browser
closes, or after 12 hours at most.

68
00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:19.049
Nothing about that computer is
remembered. Your devices are listed here.

69
00:05:19.154 --> 00:05:29.165
Each of these sends you an email, so
nothing happens without you knowing.

70
00:05:29.717 --> 00:05:32.267
Chapter 5: Your account. Download
your poems, or delete everything.

71
00:05:32.381 --> 00:05:35.551
Your poems are yours:
download everything, any time.

72
00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:42.001
Markdown to read anywhere, or a complete
JSON backup with every saved version.

73
00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:46.826
Leaving? Delete your account:
everything of yours goes, at once.

74
00:05:46.876 --> 00:05:49.808
To be sure, type your pen name.

75
00:05:49.858 --> 00:05:53.190
Done. Readers no longer
see the author anywhere.

76
00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.890
More is on the way: follow us for updates.

77
00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:00.390
InkBoard · tryinkboard.elabo.me
